If the advisor (or the University, or whomever) wants 
ownership of some particular data items, then they should
have an agreement with the student that specifies what
the delieverable data items are.

In the absence of such agreement, only the mutually
agreed-upon items (e.g. the thesis, for example) should
be in possession of the institution.

