  doggle from a trusting and uncritical alumnus, Mr. Bass decided
  he wanted his money back.
     Originally, Mr. Bass placed no restrictions as to how the pro-
  gram was to be implemented but seeing there was developing a
  distortion of his intent, Mr. Bass demanded that certain stan-
  dards be adhered to - or give me back my money.
     Yale administrators returned the gift, not being willing to
  "sacrifice or betray scholarly integrity and the principles of
  academic freedom".  There`is more but not of interest to me.
